<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imperial and Royal Army</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as k.u.k., kaiserlich und königlich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Imperial and Royal Army was the common army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, known by the abbreviation k.u.k. (kaiserlich und königlich). It drew soldiers from all the monarchy's nationalities and used German as its command language. Alongside it the Austrian and Hungarian halves maintained their own territorial forces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imperial-and-royal-army.jpg" alt="Imperial and Royal Army" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gaj777 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bielsko-Bia%C5%82a,_Garnizon_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
